<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Turkmen Feb natgas output falls six pct to 3.59 bc.</title>
<headline>Turkmen Feb natgas output falls six pct to 3.59 bc.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkmenistan's production of natural gas fell in February to 3.59 billion cubic metres from 3.81 bcm in January, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures for energy output in its latest monthly statistical bulletin. (Figures in thousands of tonnes, except for natural gas, which is in billion cubic meters) -</p>
<p> TURKMEN ENERGY OUTPUT    Feb '97	Jan '97	Jan-Feb '97</p>
<p> Natural gas		    3.59	   3.81	     7.40</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	 -5.90	 +37.80	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	  n/a	   +4.60	    +2.40</p>
<p> Crude oil		    296.2	  330.0	    626.20</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	-10.20	  -3.50	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	  n/a	   +3.70	    +0.40</p>
<p> Gasoline			39.50	  38.80	    78.30</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	 +1.80	 -36.60	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	  n/a	  -25.80	   -25.50</p>
<p> Diesel			  92.10	  97.00	   189.10</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	 -5.10	  -3.00	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	  n/a	   -8.70	   -16.70</p>
<p> Fuel oil		     134.40	 140.30	   274.70</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	 -4.20	 +35.70	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	  n/a	   +9.30	    +1.20</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
